{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation","id":907135,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Veiled Arts of Heaven : Prismatic Arrangement of Creation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-04T09:39:05-07:00","id":907135,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Veiled Arts of Heaven : Prismatic Arrangement of Creation","content":"<b>Veiled Arts of Heaven</b><br /> In addition to the traditional forms of Martial Arts practiced in Creation, the Sidereal Exalted practice a collection of secret arts and enlightened techniques, which are collectively known as Sidereal Martial Arts or the Veiled Arts of Heaven. Until recently, no member of the Exalted Host could learn Sidereal Martial Arts without either being a Sidereal, or being tutored by one- even then, only Solars could match their sifus. It is assumed that Death\u2019s Lawgivers could likewise be trained, but thus far, no Sidereal is known to have taken such a pupil.<br /> <br /> Recently, Rakan Thulio has boasted that the Getiman Exalted outstrip the Chosen of the Maidens in both mastery and enlightenment. That these mysterious Chosen have exhibited secret techniques and enlightened arts comparable to the Sidereals themselves testifies to the impossible truth of this boast. Whether the Getiman Exalted are truly capable of independent mastery of Sidereal Martial Arts, or if they, like the Solars, are simply capable of being taught and have a willing sifu in Rakan Thulio is not known- but it is certain that these mysterious Chosen are capable of matching the Sidereal Exalted\u2019s peerless mastery in one form or another.<br /> <br /> Each Sidereal and Getimian Exalted is capable of internalizing one Sidereal Martial Arts charm per dot of Essence she possesses. Solars and Abyssals are capable of internalizing one Sidereal Martial Arts charm per dot of Essence they possess above two; that is, they can learn 1 charm at Essence 3, a second charm at Essence 4, and a third at Essence 5. Additionally, all Exalted capable of learning Sidereal Martial Arts charms can learn one charm per traditional style which they have mastered. Wushu Arts, already blending two truths into one, neither hinder or assist the martial artist\u2019s ability to internalize the more fundamental ideas within the Hidden Arts of Heaven.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Martial Arts do not have a distinct ability rating like When a Sidereal Martial Arts charm calls for a martial arts roll, the martial artist may select which martial art ability they are using to execute the action.<br /> <br /> <b>PRISMATIC ARRANGEMENT OF CREATION</b><br /> The Prismatic Arrangement of Creation is assumed to be the first of the Veiled Arts of Heaven discovered; it expresses the fundamental truths of Creation through the Essence of the martial artist, allowing them to reflect and direct that power. Many sifus consider this to be an excellent first style to learn; the Forms of Creation each synergize well with most of the Unveiled Arts, and allow potent and unique expressions of martial power on both attack and defense- a perfect blending of the practical and philosophical.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons and Armor:</b> Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Forms may not be assumed if the martial artist bears any non-Natural weapons and is incompatible with armor.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Four Magical Materials Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The martial artist knows the future hidden within starmetal; she has learned the dance hidden in moonsilver; she has braved the heat of the volcano-forge from which orihalcum rises; she has befriended the five authorities of jade. With these truths, she transforms herself into a living artifact.<br /> While the martial artist is in the Four Magical Materials Form, treat her unarmed attacks as paired medium artifact hand to hand weapons with the Lethal, Brawl, Grappling, Martial Arts, Natural and Piercing tags. Increase her natural soak by +8, and increase her Hardness to 7 if it is less than 7.<br /> As a living artifact, the martial artist may even develop evocations as they are draw more deeply on the bond between themselves and the four magical materials.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: If the martial artist takes three consecutive turns during combat using miscellaneous actions discarding weapons, armor, and any artifacts she carries, she may reflexively assume the Four Magical Materials Form at the end of the third action.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Manse and Demense Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The martial artist sees with eyes closed; she hears the essence of the world, and tastes the flow of power as it moves in, around and through her. She has swum naked in the dragon lines of Creation, and can call those lines of power to her. When she enters the Manse and Demense Form, her eyes are each replaced with standard Hearthstones, while a greater hearthstone blossoms upon her forehead. The three hearthstones which appear represent the martial artist's inner self and connection to Creation; they should be selected when the charm is purchased, but may be changed with the storyteller's approval if the character of the martial artist changes dramatically. Her hearthstone eyes function as normal eyes; if the martial artist is normally blind due to lack of or damage to her eyes, then she will be able to see normally while she remains in this Form.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: If the martial artist takes three consecutive turns during combat acting with her eyes closed and using a miscellaneous action to meditate upon the nature of Creation, she may reflexively assume the Manse and Demense Form at the end of the third action.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Soul Fire Shaper Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The martial artist does not know power, any more than she knows herself. Instead she is power, drawing strength from the cold white flame of her higher soul and the hot black flame of her lower soul. She holds both fires close to her heart, and ignites into a bonfire of power. When she assumes Soul Fire Shaper Form, the martial artist's anima rises to iconic, and personal motes she spends contribute to her anima as if they were periphereal.<br /> While she is in the Soul Fire Shaper Form, the martial artist treats any references to her Essence for calculating the effects of a charm or other power as being one greater than it is, and may substitute her enhanced Essence for any other attribute or ability which has a lower rating. This does not give the martial artist access to powers she could not normally reach; for example, a Solar at Essence 2 in the Soul Fire Shaper Form would not gain the Mastery benefit of Kindly Sifu's Quill (Exalted p. 445), which requires Essence 3; nor can she purchase or otherwise access powers which require Essence greater than her noraml rating. However, it does increase any other effect which consider the martial artist's attributes or abilities, such as the Sidereal or Solar dice caps, charms such as Striking Cobra Technique (Exalted p. 427), sorcerous spells such as Death of Obsidian Butterflies (Exalted p. 472), or even Evocations such as Sinuous Liquid Escape (Exalted p. 608).<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: Any time the martial artist's anima goes from dim to iconic in a single action, she may reflexively assume the Soul Fire Shaper Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Exaltation Ways Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 12m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> The martial artist meditates on the fusion of divine and mortal forms, which come together in the Exaltation. Her mind traces the lives and mysteries of the Incarnae, of the Fire Extigent, and the Second Breath. With this understanding, she can draw upon any and all of the powers of the Exalted Host; as she does so, an appropriate caste or aspect marking will briefly shimmer on or before her, fading in the action after she assumes the form. When the martial artist enters Exaltation Ways Form, she may gains access to the anima abilities of one other caste or aspect of Exalted. For example, when Uzuki, Sidereal and Chosen of Battles, enters the Exaltation Ways Form, she may gain the anima abilities of a Dawn Caste Solar (Exalted p. 175) as well as her own anima powers as a Chosen of Battles. The martial artist may switch the anima abilities she has access to by taking a miscellaneous action and spending a point of willpower. She may only use the anima abilities after she has been in the presence of an Exalt with his anima raised to iconic, but once known such an anima is always accessible.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: Whenever the martial artist is within Medium range of another Exalt who's anima reaches Iconic for the first time in a scene, she may reflexively enter Exaltation Ways Form, matching the caste or aspect of the Exalted who inspired her.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 18m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Four Magical Materials Form, Manse and Demense Form, Soul Fire Shaper Form, Exaltation Ways Form<br /> <br /> The martial artist closes her eyes, and vanishes. She exists Elsewhere for two turns, becoming one with all things. When she returns, she returns clothed in majesty, accompanied by the scent of cherry blossoms and fresh cut palm. While she is in the Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form, the martial artist may either gain the benefit of any two charms she knows with the Form keyword, or all four of the Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form charms.<br /> Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form has no special activation rules.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T06:38:19-07:00","id":907596,"title":"","content":"This is interesting idea, but I don't think I like this take on Sidereal Martial Arts - I personally would prefer old take on Styles with longer Charm tree encompassing entire concept, which Solars and their pers would be able to learn. At the same time peerless ability of Sidereal would be expressed by their ability to add few personal Charms (your mechanics looks interesting for that) to their most internalized styles - as their personal take on secrets and truths represented by Style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew/rewrites:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/882274-new-spell-and-some-2nd-edition-spells-rewrite-for-3rd-edition-peach\" target=\"_blank\">2nd-&gt;3rd Edition Sorcery Spells Rewrite</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=890192#post890192\" target=\"_blank\">Talisman of Ten Thousand Eyes Evocations</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/913443-occult-sorcery-charms-homebrew-peach\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Occult Charms for Sorcerers</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/903155-peach-solar-thrown-charms-for-different-fighting-style-11-charms\" target=\"_blank\">Solar Thrown Charms (with Solar Danmaku Charms)</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11704-daerian","name":"Daerian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11704_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T07:48:40-07:00","id":907632,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Daerian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=907596#post907596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is interesting idea, but I don't think I like this take on Sidereal Martial Arts - I personally would prefer old take on Styles with longer Charm tree encompassing entire concept, which Solars and their pers would be able to learn. At the same time peerless ability of Sidereal would be expressed by their ability to add few personal Charms (your mechanics looks interesting for that) to their most internalized styles - as their personal take on secrets and truths represented by Style.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, fair enough! However, here's some considerations that led me down this path;<br /> <br /> A) I think we can safely assume that Sidereal Martial Arts aren't going to be super high essence Charms this go around. It's *possible* that they'll be Essence 6+ requirements on the reg, but that would be fighting the developer's stated intent to reel the game back towards the 1 to 5 range. Similarly, they could just all cluster at the Essence 3-5 range, but that would be, like, *super* akward and result in a kind of 'must eat your meat before you can have any pudding'.<br /> B) One of Jenna's original goals for SMA was to let them act in the 'secret forbidden technique' niche of wuxia movies and shonen anime. Hence why all the pre-form charms have relatively few restrictions, but the form charms and beyond require having mastered at least one other martial art.<br /> C) If Sidereal Martial Arts are strictly balanced for their Essence level, then they won't feel nearly as special; they need to be pushed, to make Sidereal teachers feel awesome and desired.<br /> D) If Sidereal Martial Arts are pushed for their Essence level, they need to have some kind of limitation to ensure / justify buying other charms- sort of the same issue that Solar xp is intended to solve, mitigating the bad-feel of spending experience on something *other* than Charms- but preferribly while still avoiding (or at least mitigating) the bad feel mentioned in point A.<br /> <br /> This solution enables most Sidereal characters, even from out the gate, to have *their* super cool secret technique- without allowing Sidereal Martial Arts to be overwhelming in their presence or volume. Plus, it lets each effect be signature and *big*- without the arms race that eventually led to 2E's 'Infinite Shards of WTF'<br /> <br /> Now; is this the only solution? Oh, *hell* no! It's not even the only solution if you agree with all the steps that led to it, let alone if you disagree with those axioms!<br /> <br /> But I feel like it's a viable and interesting solution, and so it's one I intend to run down for Where Fate Has Led, until persuaded that there are flaws beyond personal taste <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:25:43-07:00","id":907883,"title":"","content":"I don't mind the simple ideas, in fact I like them. My only real issue is with the special activations. I mean they are flavourful, but at the same time spending 3 actions basically doing nothing vs a single turn throwing up my form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T14:44:48-07:00","id":907897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=907883#post907883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't mind the simple ideas, in fact I like them. My only real issue is with the special activations. I mean they are flavourful, but at the same time spending 3 actions basically doing nothing vs a single turn throwing up my form.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Eh?<br /> Four Magical Materials Form requires three turns taking misc actions tossing away weapons and armor- but miscellancious combat actions can be flurried.<br /> Manse and Demense Form requires acting for three turns with your eyes shut.<br /> Soul Fire Shaper Form requires going from Dim to Iconic in a single action.<br /> And Exaltation Ways Form is- well, it's just basically out of your hands.<br /> <br /> (Now, Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form does just eat three turns of doing nothing, I'll give you that one, and I'm honestly on the fence about how long you should be stuck elsewhere before returning as a bodhisattva of ass kicking)- but none of the special activation forms require doing nothing for three turns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:08:49-07:00","id":907910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=907897#post907897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Eh?<br /> Four Magical Materials Form requires three turns taking misc actions tossing away weapons and armor- but miscellancious combat actions can be flurried.<br /> Manse and Demense Form requires acting for three turns with your eyes shut.<br /> Soul Fire Shaper Form requires going from Dim to Iconic in a single action.<br /> And Exaltation Ways Form is- well, it's just basically out of your hands.<br /> <br /> (Now, Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form does just eat three turns of doing nothing, I'll give you that one, and I'm honestly on the fence about how long you should be stuck elsewhere before returning as a bodhisattva of ass kicking)- but none of the special activation forms require doing nothing for three turns.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I find the first one a bit more interesting in a sense, as it conjures images of a stripper ninja which amuse me, but at the same time it involves a lot of complexity. No surprise that SMA should have a lot of complexity, but the three turns should be spent accomplishing *something* at least. That something being an interesting goal, rather than a single misc action that accomplishes a minor fluff bit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:11:34-07:00","id":907917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=907910#post907910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I find the first one a bit more interesting in a sense, as it conjures images of a stripper ninja which amuse me, but at the same time it involves a lot of complexity. No surprise that SMA should have a lot of complexity, but the three turns should be spent accomplishing *something* at least. That something being an interesting goal, rather than a single misc action that accomplishes a minor fluff bit.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can flurry the misc actions- you can still do *anything* else.<br /> I feel like we must be talking past one another in some way- you keep talking about three turns accomplishing nothing, but that's only the case if you don't flurry those actions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"us