,"avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T15:54:17-07:00","id":907945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=907944#post907944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll make a post about what I mean after my game, but right now I need to head towards it as its about to start.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Fair enough!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T20:32:20-07:00","id":908075,"title":"","content":"OK what I meant was for most of the MA forms, all of them require you doing a very active component.<ul><li>Snake needs you make an enemy's initiative from greater than your own to less.</li> <li>Tiger wants you to deal a big, meaty piece of damage.</li> <li>Shining Point wants you to win initiative</li> <li>White Reaper wants you to be surrounded and outnumbered.</li> <li>Ebon Shadow simply wants you to beat opponents in a contested stealth roll</li> <li>Crane is similar to Snake</li> <li>Nightengale wants people to listen to your song</li> <li>Righteous Devil wants you to nail someone and be an accurate shot in doing so</li> <li>Dreaming Pearl wants you to remain elusive as a dream, thus disengaging activates the form.</li> </ul>And so on. Each of these are something you not only can do in combat, but are fun and something that should be encouraged. You often don't need to flurry, making yourself worse at rolls. They're things you generally want to do, or think about how to pull off in the areas such as Crane and Black Claw. Yours are just things such as &quot;Spend 3 turns with your eyes closed&quot;, &quot;Three turns taking off armour&quot;. It may be thematic but what does this accomplish mechanically? How does this entice the player to make a specific playstyle? The only thing it does is make the carrot that is normally dynamic forms into a stick to beat yourself with. Fire Shaper form and Exaltation Ways is fine, but I'd probably reform Five Magical Materials and Manse and Demense form.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T05:02:31-07:00","id":908265,"title":"","content":"Hm.<br /> <br /> On the one hand, I grok. I see what you mean by 'doing nothing'.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Prismatic Arrangement of Creation- at least the Four Magical Materials branch and the Manse and Demense branch -were never super... flavorful, in how they lead the character to fight. They are very generic 'martial artist t'ai chi katas'.<br /> <br /> I'll give this a ponder. If I (or you, or anyone) can suggest special activations that would fit thematically and inspire more interesting choices, I'm open to 'em- half the reason I post this stuff on the forum is to steal ideas I like more <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T19:41:58-07:00","id":934246,"title":"","content":"Question: If you use Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form to do Single Point Shining into the Void Form and Obsidian Shards of Infinity Form does that allow 4 attacks a turn, or does that not work due to Weapon Restrictions?<br /> <br /> Other question: Can you use Worn weapons with Prismatic Arrangement of Creation charms?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-19T22:41:45-07:00","id":934305,"title":"","content":"My objection to this is that all other martial arts follow a progression of two to three foundation Charms, possibly one or two more successor Charms, a Form Charm. possibly one or two following on from that, and a capstone. Four Magical Materials Style is two layers, no capstone, and consists entirely of Form Charms. Charms which I consider badly overpowered for Essence 1, by the way. If you want to make Sidereal martial arts more powerful, then make them higher Essence as well. Most Martial Arts Charms are Essence 3 or lower, so there's available design space to work in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1184-ladylens","name":"LadyLens","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T07:05:12-07:00","id":934467,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=934246#post934246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Question: If you use Prismatic Arrangement of Creation Form to do Single Point Shining into the Void Form and Obsidian Shards of Infinity Form does that allow 4 attacks a turn, or does that not work due to Weapon Restrictions?<br /> <br /> Other question: Can you use Worn weapons with Prismatic Arrangement of Creation charms?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't work due to weapon restrictions- Single Point requires you to be using a single slashing sword, Obsidian Shards allows for paired weapons, and Prismatic Arrangement is strictly unarmed.<br /> <br /> And no, you can't use Worn weapons with Prismatic Arrangement, only weapons with the Natural tag.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LadyLens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=934305#post934305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My objection to this is that all other martial arts follow a progression of two to three foundation Charms, possibly one or two more successor Charms, a Form Charm. possibly one or two following on from that, and a capstone. Four Magical Materials Style is two layers, no capstone, and consists entirely of Form Charms. Charms which I consider badly overpowered for Essence 1, by the way. If you want to make Sidereal martial arts more powerful, then make them higher Essence as well. Most Martial Arts Charms are Essence 3 or lower, so there's available design space to work in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, this gets into the essence of my approach towards Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> One of Jenna's ideas for how Sidereal Martial Arts were to be used in play was to be the 'super secret technique' that a character may only know one of at the start of the series, and the learning of which is always a notable achievement. Her means of accomplishing this was by allowing Sidereals to learn SMA form charms only after mastering a Celestial Martial Art- enabling characters to start with a handful of such charms, but not being able to depend on them.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, this created a weird incentive to rush completion of a single CMA in order to unlock buying complete Sidereal Martial Arts- so they became less secret techniques and more gated powers. Additionally, one of the primary means that SMAs were used to illustrate power was in being the only primary source of Essence 6+ combat charms for a *very* long time. That's basically a no-go in Exalted 3e, which is explicitly walking back from the Essence 6+ space.<br /> <br /> My approach is to instead limit the absolute number of SMA Charms a character can learn- making each one learned more character defining. In exchange for this limitation, they are pushed in power relative to their Essence requirement. This also requires the SMA be more condensed and focused relative to past incarnations- whereas the original Prismatic Arrangement of Creation was... around 16ish Charms, the things people remember about it are the multiple forms and the ultimate form breaking one of the cardinal rules established thus far, of only allowing a single Martial Arts form to be active at once. So, my version focuses on that element, bringing it strongly into the foreground.<br /> <br /> Now, you are free to disagree with that approach, and instead say that Sidereal Martial Arts should 'just' be higher Essence minimum Martial Arts charms which can only be learned by Sidereals, Getimians, Solars and Abyssals. I do not believe that is a profitable avenue to explore, but would be willing to see what such a conversion would look like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:04:21-07:00","id":934635,"title":"","content":"Sort of was going to comment back in April but didn't (unless I did elsewhere in another thread and have forgotten it! which is entirely possible) is part of the argument around around letting characters learn a finite set of SMA Charms is, back when they were introduced in 1e, part of the in setting rationale for why SMA exist was that:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Martial arts do not have the same limitations as ordinary Sidereal Charms. For the Sidereal Exalted they offer a route to large combat dice pools, mote-efficient Charms, new Charms and high-Essence Charms. In addition, creatures outside of Fate have no such resistance to Sidereal Martial Arts.<br /> <br /> A very long time ago, the older Sidereal Exalted decided that this was <b>interesting.</b>&quot;</i><br /> <br /> So if you do go with a literally finite number of SMA Charms that can be learned per character (leaving aside whether SMA each contain a few big things or many smaller things), as opposed to being practically finite through costs or something, it seems you are kind of scaling back on that idea, inevitably to some degree, that SMA is the free / open set of Sidereal Charms that Sidereals can exploit to get as many new Charms as they like that are lacking in their set, so long as they fit the SMA aesthetic (which I guess I would say is being more or less, strikes and katas and holds, and blocks and dodges, of a sort?) and they hang together as a style.<br /> <br /> That's not a reason not to go this way exactly, but might be something people might love... or hate, I think depending on how much they are serious about the limit of Sidereal Charms really should be that the set is finite, or that actually that's not really meant to be so hard a limit as something for Sidereals to overcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T12:39:28-07:00","id":934651,"title":"","content":"Eeehhhhhhhhh.<br /> <br /> I mean- yes and no.<br /> <br /> Sidereal Martial Arts, and Martial Arts in general, are still 'open' in a way that the Sidereal Charms aren't; you can invent a new style to let you do whatever you want / need to do in a relatively straightforward fashion, as long as whatever you want / need to do involves punching.<br /> <br /> The limitation I'm placing is on how many Sidereal Martial Arts charms a given individual can learn, not how many can exist; on top of which, it's a limit you *can* cheat, given infinite experience, by letting someone learn additional SMA charms per completed Martial Art.<br /> <br /> (Plus, the 'older Sidereal Exalted decided this was interesting' feeds into SMA as being primarily very high essence charms, which I don't feel is a profitable area to explore)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-20T16:13:49-07:00","id":934762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=934467#post934467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It doesn't work due to weapon restrictions- Single Point requires you to be using a single slashing sword, Obsidian Shards allows for paired weapons, and Prismatic Arrangement is strictly unarmed.<br /> <br /> And no, you can't use Worn weapons with Prismatic Arrangement, only weapons with the Natural tag.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC you can use paired slashing swords with Single Point, which allows you to use Steel Devil with it. But the Prismatic Arrangement restriction would still disallow it.<br /> <br /> Also, Worn weapons are treated has having the Natural Tag while being worn, IIRC. <br /> <br /> I went and found the wording: <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Worn: Wearable weapons can be removed, but while worn<br /> they count as natural weapons. Equipping or removing a<br /> weapon with the worn tag takes an action. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T06:50:53-07:00","id":935033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=934762#post934762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> IIRC you can use paired slashing swords with Single Point, which allows you to use Steel Devil with it. But the Prismatic Arrangement restriction would still disallow it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eeeh. The form weapons for Single Point don't explicitly call out using paired weapons. I could see the arguement, but probably wouldn't allow it at my table<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aranfan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=934762#post934762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, Worn weapons are treated has having the Natural Tag while being worn, IIRC.<br /> <br /> I went and found the wording:</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, be damned. I thought that Worn just meant they couldn't be disarmed. Not entirely sure how I feel about that- something feels incongrous with the t'ai chi master using brass knuckles or wearing a razor harness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T16:01:43-07:00","id":935323,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/907135-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-prismatic-arrangement-of-creation?p=935033#post935033\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eeeh. The form weapons for Single Point don't explicitly call out using paired weapons. I could see the arguement, but probably wouldn't allow it at my table</div> </div> </div> </div>It does use the plural tho', and if you can't use it with paired weapons than you can't use Steel Devil with it, leaving Single Point the only style in the core book that can't benefit from knowing another style.<br /> <br /> But I guess it's pretty academic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11917-aranfan","name":"Aranfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11917_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"503"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}